Subject: [PATCH 4/6] src/lab-process-mail: Run each pass in its own workspace
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: uqtwswqpstmkzqzqnswpponryxnpkzpo

Each pass ran in the trunk workspace, and the agent moves its working
copy freely: it starts fresh changes on trunk or b/dev, and leaves the
workspace wherever its last series ended. The operator came back to a
different working copy than the one they left, and anything they had
in progress there was left behind on some other commit.

The agent now gets a workspace of its own, created on first use and
brought up to date before every pass. Commits are shared through the
one repo, so nothing it produces is lost, but its working copy can no
longer disturb anyone else.
